WEBVTT

00:09:58.218 --> 00:10:00.012
in particular, gas more recently.

00:10:00.012 --> 00:10:01.180
And pipelines.

00:10:01.555 --> 00:10:02.806
You've written about this.

00:10:02.848 --> 00:10:06.560
You feel very strongly about this
as a young African climate activist.

00:10:06.602 --> 00:10:07.895
Tell us more.

00:10:07.936 --> 00:10:10.856
VN: Yes, there is a very big challenge

00:10:10.898 --> 00:10:14.318
that so many African nations
are facing right now.

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:18.447
There is a pressure to transition
to renewable energy.

00:10:18.489 --> 00:10:22.701
There's a pressure to lift people
out of energy poverty.

00:10:22.701 --> 00:10:26.038
But then there is no climate
finance to do that.

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:29.541
So what is happening
is that fossil fuel companies

00:10:29.583 --> 00:10:35.005
are coming with all these deals
for the gas or for the oil